 still plausible", "Steroid-induced myopathy: Presents with isolated weakness without sensory loss or pain"], "alarm_features": ["Significant unintentional weight loss", "Systemic hypertension", "Chronic tobacco use", "Diabetes mellitus"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Brachial Plexopathy and Related Disorders", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.12751404488584167, "posterior": 0.1230952434607679, "danger": 0.2, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Subacute timeline moderately favors brachial plexopathy over aggressive malignancies that would progress more rapidly."], "evidence_against": ["Systemic features like hypertension and diabetes provide the strongest counterpoint to isolated plexopathy diagnosis."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3", "B1.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.1, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Thoracic Outlet Syndrome", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.089, "danger": 0.15, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of documented trauma moderately disfavors traumatic brachial plexopathy, even in the context of bodybuilding and steroid use."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Thoracic Malignancy with Nerve Compression", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.08422440517042595, "posterior": 0.07996212731709954, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Subacute timeline moderately favors brachial plexopathy over aggressive malignancies that would progress more rapidly."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Cerebrovascular Disease", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.027, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Subacute progression is inconsistent with typical acute stroke presentation, mildly supporting alternative diagnoses."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Other Systemic or Neurological Disorders", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.027, "danger": 0.1, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Traumatic Brachial Plexopathy", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.074, "danger": 0.1, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of documented trauma moderately disfavors traumatic brachial plexopathy, even in the context of bodybuilding and steroid use."]}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Neoplastic Brachial Plexopathy (e.g., Pancoast Tumor)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.033, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Subacute progression weakly supports inflammatory/idiopathic plexopathy, moderately reduces neoplastic likelihood."]}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Paraneoplastic Brachial Plexopathy", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.009, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of paraneoplastic signs weakly disfavors paraneoplastic plexopathy, though this is less definitive than neoplastic variants."]}, "B1.4": {"id": "B1.4", "label": "Inflammatory/Idiopathic Brachial Plexopathy", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.006, "danger": 0.1, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B3.1": {"id": "B3.1", "label": "Apical Lung Tumor (Pancoast Tumor) with Brachial Plexus Compression", "level": 2, "s